cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or a dataset generated with it, please cite it as below."
title: "PnPCorrespondences: Synthetic 2D-3D Point Correspondences for Camera Calibration and PnP Benchmarking"
abstract: >-
  A generator and benchmark suite for large, systematic, image-free datasets of
  2D-3D point correspondences with exact ground truth. It synthesises structured
  3D scenes, samples camera intrinsics and look-at poses for pinhole,
  Brown-Conrady and Kannala-Brandt models, applies controlled Gaussian pixel
  noise, quantization and outlier contamination, and serialises everything to
  HDF5 with a Parquet manifest. It also ships fifteen classical and modern PnP
  solvers, single-view and multi-view calibration baselines, evaluation metrics,
  summary tables and figures, so that camera calibration, Perspective-n-Point
  solvers, robust estimators and bundle adjustment can be benchmarked against
  absolute ground truth.
type: software
